Tested with the following sample project:
[testdocs_2026-06-22_19-08-26.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29203026/testdocs_2026-06-22_19-08-26.zip)


And identified some issues, there are more if you compare it against the same GDScript implementations:

### 1. Double rendered summary blocks

```xml
/// <summary>
/// Inspector documentation test surface for <see cref="NewScript"/>.
/// This class mixes Godot export patterns such as ranges, flags, file paths,
/// node paths, resources, arrays, and grouped properties to exercise the C#
/// XML documentation rendering added for editor tooltips and generated docs.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// The inspector should preserve inline references like <see cref="WeaponSlot"/>,
/// <see cref="DefaultDisplayName"/>, and inline code such as
/// <code>[ExportGroup("Combat")].</code>
/// </remarks>
public partial class NewScript : Node
```

The description is rendered twice for the comments above:

<img width="1083" height="438" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ad4a880-d761-491f-bd1c-22051f74c2cc" />

### 2. Alphabetically ordered properties/fields

<img width="637" height="697" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d36c823a-a06c-4de9-9f69-72495f7d3255" />

The exported member should preserve their original order-of-declaration in documentation

### 3. Typed Godot Collections not properly handled

```csharp
public Godot.Collections.Array<Vector3> PatrolPoints { get; set; } =
public Godot.Collections.Dictionary<string, Vector2> NamedCheckpoints { get; set; } = new()
public float[] NamedWaveforms { get; set; } = new float[] { 0.0f, 0.5f, 1.0f, 0.5f, 0.0f };
public Godot.Collections.Array<PackedScene> InventoryScenes { get; set; } = [];
```

The following exported member declaration should be:
```gdscript
Array[Vector3] PatrolPoints
Dictionary[String, Vector2] NamedCheckpoints
Array[float] NamedWaveforms
Array[PackedScene] InventoryScenes
```

instead of

<img width="500" height="161" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1fc5747c-c46b-4aee-94e8-3a0c037bc3a0" />

Hello, and thanks for this! I've applied this as a patch on top of my Godot 4.6 and it's working great already, it's amazing how helpful it is.

Here are a few bugs I found:

#### 1. New lines in description parts (like text between `<summary>` tags or `<param>` tags) will be converted to `<br>`, which is not wanted. `<br>` should only be inserted if there is an empty line between two paragraphs.
Example of the problem:
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// This is a long line, too long to fit unwrapped in a code editor, right? Let's wrap
/// it in the source code file. If I
/// wrap it here, it creates too many new lines.
/// </summary>
[GlobalClass]
public partial class ...
```
Looks like this (added arrows to show the line breaks that are persisted):
<img width="695" height="151" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/61c33480-5478-40f7-8b9b-1633fb2ed34c" />
<img width="690" height="238" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a8b6ed3-132c-4656-985a-6b2c99f6940f" />
<hr>

#### 2. Clicking on the Docs button next to a component's name opens the default Node documentation, instead of the documentation page for the C# class of the component.
<img width="508" height="142" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/24ee52e2-5c6f-4198-996a-67b4571ecbb2" />
<hr>

#### 3. Class description, remarks are not properly written on doc page. Seealsos are not displayed at all for classes Bold text followed by code text is not spaced nor appearing correctly:
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Here is some description. Here is some description. Here is some description. Here is some description.
/// Here is some description. Here is some description. Here is some description. Here is some description.
/// </summary>
///
/// <remarks>
/// ⚠️ To compare if two entity variables <c>A</c> and <c>B</c> are holding the same entity, <b>DO NOT USE</b> <c>A == B</c>.
/// </remarks>
///
/// <seealso cref="FLCore.GetEntity"/>
[GlobalClass]
public partial class ...
```
<img width="917" height="306" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/856eca0b-eefe-44c4-9b52-9da16504a638" />
